    "result_text": "You can now give a job a short description when you add it, and it shows on the job's page. `bin/e2e` builds and the acceptance test passes. I haven't tried adding a job with a description through the form, and I didn't run any other tests.\n\n- **Database:** a new migration, `V35__project_description.sql`, adds an optional `description` column (up to 500 characters) to the job table.\n- **Server:**\n  - Jobs now carry a description. When you add a job, the description is optional, trimmed, limited to 500 characters, and left empty if blank.\n  - The job details sent to the front end include it.\n  - The test-data seeding endpoint now accepts `description` on jobs.\n- **Front end:**\n  - The add-job form has an optional \"Description\" text box (`project-form-description`), with an error message if it goes over 500 characters (`project-form-description-error`).\n  - The job's page shows the description under the name with `data-testid=\"job-description\"`, but only when there is one.\n\nThere's no way yet to add or change the description of an existing job.",
